# Copy to .env. Values here are the starting values; the console's Settings page
# can change them (see the README's Configuration table). A commented line is
# off and shows its default. Under Docker Compose nothing here is required: the
# store is wired in, without an RPC nothing is read, and without an Etherscan
# key SCC AU and AC report themselves not run. Outside Compose, set
# WASHTRACE_STORE_URL: the worker will not start without it, and the API answers 503.

# The Postgres database washtrace creates its schema in. Compose sets its own
# and ignores this one. DATABASE_URL is read if this is unset.
# WASHTRACE_STORE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/washtrace

# One JSON-RPC URL per chain, WASHTRACE_RPC_<chainId>. Any provider (Alchemy,
# Infura, QuickNode) or your own node. Finding a collection's deployment block
# needs archive state; give fromBlock when adding it if yours has none.
WASHTRACE_RPC_1=
# WASHTRACE_RPC_8453=

# Etherscan API V2: one key for every chain. https://etherscan.io/apidashboard
WASHTRACE_ETHERSCAN_KEY=
# Calls a second. Default 4; the free plan allows 5.
# WASHTRACE_ETHERSCAN_RPS=
# Any API that answers Etherscan's account actions, such as Blockscout. Default
# is Etherscan V2. While the key comes from here and none is saved in the
# console, a URL saved in the console is ignored, so it cannot receive the key.
# WASHTRACE_ETHERSCAN_URL=

# HTTP basic auth over every page and API route but /api/health. Set both or neither.
# Without it, settings can be saved only from this machine.
# WASHTRACE_USERNAME=
# WASHTRACE_PASSWORD=

# Hops of money the worker follows out of a trader, so SCC AU can see a
# payment routed back through wallets that never traded. Default 3, at most 10;
# 0 reads traders only.
# WASHTRACE_FOLLOW_HOPS=

# Read a trader's money and other tokens again when it trades, at most once
# every N days (0–365); 0 (default) is off. Each re-read is about 4 Etherscan calls.
# WASHTRACE_FOLLOW_REREAD=

# on: the token read also reads the tokens of wallets traders paid in them, up
# to 25 more reads per trader. Anything but "on" is off.
# WASHTRACE_TOKENS_PAYEES=

# The Hugging Face dataset (owner/name) stored data is downloaded from. Default
# jonathanmiro97/washtrace-data. `npm run publish:hub` also publishes to it.
# WASHTRACE_STORED_REPO=
# Where the worker keeps stored data. Default data/stored; /app/data/stored in
# the images.
# WASHTRACE_STORED_DIR=

# The port Compose publishes the console and API on, on 127.0.0.1. Default 8080.
# WASHTRACE_PORT=
# The worker's health check port. Default 8081.
# WASHTRACE_WORKER_PORT=

# Hugging Face token that can write to the dataset. Only `npm run publish:hub`
# reads it; the worker and the console never do, and reading the public
# datasets (NFT-70M too) needs none. https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
# HF_TOKEN=
